<title>CHINA: HKR Int'l year net jumps sharply.</title>
<headline>HKR Int'l year net jumps sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   109.0   vs 47.0 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    16.0    vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  nil     vs 38.6 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    1,139.9 vs 482.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		     3,910.1 vs 2,758.5</p>
<p>    Company name		 HKR International Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 24-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 16</p>
<p>NOTE - HKR International is a property investment and development company.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one new share for every 10 shares held.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted to take into account of a bonus issue of shares in the proportion of one bonus share for every 10 shares held on September 26, 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 25 H.K. cents (including interim dividend of nine cents) vs 20 cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
